cff-version: 1.2.0
title: merge-mining-research
message: "If you use this software or its datasets, please cite the project as below. Dataset licensing is documented in LICENSE-DATA."
type: software
authors:
  - name: deadmanoz
repository-code: "https://github.com/deadmanoz/merge-mining-research"
abstract: >-
  Research into Bitcoin merge mining and what it reveals about Bitcoin mining
  generally. When a sibling chain merge-mines Bitcoin, its merge-mining evidence
  can preserve the Bitcoin parent headers miners built on (canonical and
  competing) and coinbase evidence. The most developed aspect recovers
  direct-stale header candidates from that evidence, applies documented
  available-evidence validation gates, and publishes reproducible recovery
  evidence. The project also ships
  tested marker definitions for future census work on canonical-chain
  merge-mining commitments; mining-pool attribution is not part of this release.
keywords:
  - bitcoin
  - merge-mining
  - auxpow
  - stale-blocks
  - mining-pools
  - blockchain-research
